 To apply a Gaussian filter before the Sobel edge detection in MATLAB, you need to add an extra step to apply the Gaussian filter to your grayscale image. Here's how you can modify your code:
```matlab
% Read input image and convert to grayscale
input_image = imread('image.jpg');
gray_image = rgb2gray(input_image);
% Apply Gaussian filter to reduce noise
gaussian_filter = fspecial('gaussian', [3 3], 0.5); % Set standard deviation to 0.5
smoothed_image = imfilter(gray_image, gaussian_filter);
% Define Sobel operators in x and y directions
sobel_x = [-1 0 1; -2 0 2; -1 0 1];
sobel_y = [-1 -2 -1; 0 0 0; 1 2 1];
% Apply Sobel operator in x direction
edge_image_x = conv2(double(smoothed_image), sobel_x, 'same');
% Apply Sobel operator in y direction
edge_image_y = conv2(double(smoothed_image), sobel_y, 'same');
% Combine edges in both directions
edge_image = sqrt(edge_image_x.^2 + edge_image_y.^2);
% Display original image, smoothed image, and edge image
subplot(1,3,1), imshow(input_image); title('Original Image');
subplot(1,3,2), imshow(smoothed_image); title('Gaussian Filter Applied');
subplot(1,3,3), imshow(edge_image); title('Edge Detection');
```
In this modified code, we added a new line where we defined a Gaussian filter using the `fspecial` function and applied it to the grayscale image using the `imfilter` function. This filter helps reduce the noise in the image before applying the Sobel edge detection. We also added three subplots to display the original image, the smoothed image, and the edge image for better comparison.

